// MP-par-MP -- two copies of MP (MP.lit) in parallel, release-acquire.
//
// Source: Arlt & Vafeiadis, "RGSep under Release/Acquire Consistency",
//         PACMPL 10 (OOPSLA2), Article 375, 2026. doi:10.1145/3839507, Section 3: by the Par rule MP || MP has the same specification as MP.
//
// Both writers store the same values, so whichever write each reader sees, it
// has seen x = 7 before.
//
// Reference verdicts:
//   the paper: under RA neither reader sees y = 1 and then x != 7.
//   herd7 7.58 on herd/MP-par-MP.litmus, under the zoo's abstract-sc, abstract-tso,
//     ra, sra, wra and abstract-coherence cat models and herd's rc11.cat:
//     Coherence allows; SC, TSO, RA, SRA, WRA and RC11 forbid.
// The paper's registers are renamed r -> ry, b -> rb, and the second copy's
// rs, re: MoRDor reads only names beginning with r as registers.
x := 0; y := 0;
{ x.store(7, rel); y.store(1, rel) }
||| { ry := y.load(acq); rb := x.load(acq) }
||| { x.store(7, rel); y.store(1, rel) }
||| { rs := y.load(acq); re := x.load(acq) }
%%
allow ((ry = 1 && rb != 7) || (rs = 1 && re != 7)) [Coherence]
forbid ((ry = 1 && rb != 7) || (rs = 1 && re != 7)) [SC, TSO, RA, SRA, WRA, RC11]
